{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mat-20-1","title":"Matthew 20:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ, by the similitude of the labourers in the vineyard, shows that God is debtor unto no man; 17 foretells his passion; 20 by answering the mother of Zebedee's children, teaches his disciples to be lowly; 29 and gives two blind men their sight.</p>\n<p>the kingdom.This parable was intended to illustrate the equity of God's dealings, even when \"the first are placed last, and the last first.\"</p>\n<p>3:2; 13:24,31,33,44,45,47; 22:2; 25:1,14 a man. 9:37,38; 21:33-43; So 8:11,12; Isa 5:1,2; Joh 15:1 early. 23:37; So 8:11,12; Jer 25:3,4 labourers. Mr 13:34; 1Co 15:58; Heb 13:21; 2Pe 1:5-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-20-2","title":"Matthew 20:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>he had. 13; Ex 19:5,6; De 5:27-30 a penny.\"The Roman penny is the eighth part of an ounce, which after five shillings the ounce is sevenpence halfpenny.\"</p>\n<p>18:28; 22:19; *margins Lu 10:35; Re 6:6 he sent. 1Sa 2:18,26; 3:1,21; 16:11,12; 1Ki 3:6-11; 18:12; 2Ch 34:3; Ec 12:1 Lu 1:15; 2Ti 3:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-20-3","title":"Matthew 20:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>the third. Mr 15:25; Ac 2:15 standing. 6,7; 11:16,17; Pr 19:15; Eze 16:49; Ac 17:17-21; 1Ti 5:13; Heb 6:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-20-4","title":"Matthew 20:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Go. 9:9; 21:23-31; Lu 19:7-10; Ro 6:16-22; 1Co 6:11; 1Ti 1:12,13 Tit 3:8; 1Pe 1:13; 4:2,3 and whatsoever. Col 4:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mat-20-5","title":"Matthew 20:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MAT","chapterStart":20,"ve